so i usually have a script to go off of  but today i thought i'd just talk  straight from the heart this isn't the  usual content that i make on this  channel but as we're getting closer to  50 000 subscribers i found myself  thinking about the journey it took to  get to this point and i got pretty  emotional about it to say the least it's  been an absolute grind and saying that  elden ring and more accurately from  software has probably saved my life  isn't too far of a stretch so today i'm  going to talk about my life and my  content creation journey if you're  uncomfortable with discussions about  depression suicidal thoughts addiction  stuff like that then i wouldn't watch  this video and i'll see you all in the  next lore video but if you want to hear  my story then let's get started so ever  since i can remember i've always wanted  to be a content creator i used to prop  up a camcorder and record myself playing  guitar hero back when i was like 10  years old i asked my parents if i could  upload it to youtube which at the time  was a brand new website and they told me  that no one wanted to watch me play  video games so i didn't it really wasn't  cool at all to be into video games back  in those days i'm only 27 now but even  back then i sort of had to hide the fact  that i played video games my friends  really weren't into it yet and my family  just thought it was a waste of time i'm  sure that's not uncommon for a lot of  people that grew up in the early 2000s  along with this i played a ton of golf  my family wasn't rich or anything just  scraping by middle class family and my  parents thought i could go places if i  knew how to play golf so i started  playing when i was 12 my dad would take  me to a cheap driving range for me to  practice at i played junior high school  golf and actually got an offer to play  college golf at a local school i got  some other offers too but i just wanted  to stay close to home because i had been  dating a girl all through high school  and i didn't want to be too far from her  now i was not ready at all to go to  college yet i had no idea what i wanted  to major in yet and took a local offer  to play golf because that's what my  family and i had worked toward my entire  childhood if i didn't get a scholarship  then we couldn't afford college now i  could have just gone to a community  college for free and figured it out then  but i wanted to play golf so i took the  offer close to home for the 2014 school  year now college was not a good time for  me i started getting depressed because i  didn't know how to do things on my own  at this point in my life my first few  days of class i forgot to eat because i  was just running around going to class  in practice all day the life of a  college athlete is not easy you're  either in class you're at practice at a  team study hall team meetings or  required events tournaments all of that  stuff i would miss a ton of class  playing in tournaments and it would  stress me out to no end eventually i  just dropped out of college to join a  pro golf tour in orlando florida i was  out there for about three months before  i injured my right wrist i hit the back  of a tree root on a downswing and to  compare that to something if you don't  know too much about golf it's like  swinging a baseball bat as hard as you  can at a brick wall i actually wound up  doing this two different times since  it's really hard to see the roots under  the straw grass in florida and i've  still got nerve damage in my risk to  this day so i went back home to decide  what to do next also when i came home my  long-term girlfriend broke up with me i  don't want to talk about this too much  but it completely broke my heart but  after this i went to work as an  assistant pro at a local country club  where i'd give people golf lessons and  run the golf shop this was probably the  most depressing job i've ever had since  it paid next to nothing while working  super long hours with little to no  appreciation from the members of the  club but this is when i started  streaming rocket league on twitch after  work so that was kind of nice i saved up  some money to get back out there to play  pro golf and after doing some physical  therapy it took about a year but i went  back to florida but this time i played  in miami i actually stayed in some guy's  refurbished garage in a really sketchy  neighborhood in hollywood florida which  is right next to miami that had decent  internet so i could stream on the side  as well after a month into that i got  robbed at gunpoint while i was just  getting something out of my car in the  driveway they took some things out of  the car and some money from my wallet  but it definitely scared me enough to  just get the hell out of there and find  another place to play i decided to move  all the way out to arizona and they had  some golf tours out there but while  practicing i started having some pain  flare up in my wrist again so i started  some physical therapy training again and  focused on streaming rocket league for a  while i had some success streaming in  early 2019 i was coaching new players  but it definitely wasn't the content  that i wanted to make but it was the  game that i was good at and that i had  played for a few years and i thought  that that's what people wanted at the  time so i just kept doing that i was  completely alone in this apartment in an  area where i had no friends or family  and this is where my depression got a  lot worse it got to a point where i  didn't leave my apartment for well over  a month straight i didn't even go out to  get food or groceries i'd just order  from doordash or instacart and stayed in  my apartment i stopped doing physical  therapy because it didn't seem like it  was getting better  and i just stayed inside streaming i  completely abandoned golf and just spent  all my time streaming and coaching  rocket league i gained about 50 pounds  within just a few months with all of the  fast food and energy drinks i was  consuming on a daily basis and my  depression just obviously got worse and  worse and i'll be honest at this point  i did not want to live anymore i felt  like i had nothing going for me so i  actually planned on how i was going to  commit suicide i won't go into too much  detail about that but i quite literally  packed up all of my things into the  corner of my apartment so it would be  easier for people to get my things out  after they found my body it was really  bad but i decided to go on a hike  through the mountains of arizona and i  told myself that if i still wanted to  die after the hike then i could needless  to say i got to the top of the mountain  after a couple of hours saw a beautiful  sunrise after going super early to avoid  people and i felt a wave of emotions  come over me to put it short i didn't  want to die anymore likely because i was  doing something active outside of my  apartment for the first time in a while  and it felt really good i called my  family i told them everything and my mom  caught the first flight out that she  could so that she could drive all the  way back to missouri with me this was  the start of 2020 and i vowed to myself  to get back out into the world and  experience all it had to offer for me  well we all know what happened in 2020.  basically it was impossible to live up  to that promise i made for myself  because of the pandemic but at least i  was surrounded by family which made it  better than just being alone the first  thing i did when i got back was adopt a  dog her name is joy and she's literally  the best dog i could ever ask for taking  care of her and myself made life so much  more enjoyable i started exercising and  eating right and i can happily say that  i've lost all of that weight and then  some and i'm currently in the best shape  i've ever been in and it feels amazing  there's a lot of things that can cure  depression but in my opinion i think  exercise and just eating correctly  taking care of your body and your mind  is the best way to do it around this  time in 2020 is when a new hot game  called valrant released and i was pretty  addicted to it off the start i decided  to upload a tutorial on a new cool trick  i learned with the character omen  and to put it short it absolutely popped  off a few videos later in a few hundred  thousand views and i was the early omen  maine of valorant on youtube i made  about two dozen videos under the name  jake from state farm and got my channel  to around 20 000 subscribers now that's  not this channel i actually deleted my  valrant channel after just not enjoying  the game anymore and anything else that  i uploaded like a different game  none of my subscribers ever wanted to  see it they would just ask for more  valerian stuff i was a little spiteful  at the time and just deleted the channel  but i just didn't want to play the game  anymore so i didn't really care i went  on a short bout of variety streaming on  twitch just playing random games that i  wanted to play and i found little to no  success with that eventually i went back  to streaming rocket league i felt like  it was the only content i could make  that could be of some value to people  now i didn't want to do this but rocket  league around this time was going free  to play soon so i thought i'd give it  another shot but rocket league  absolutely skyrocketed in popularity  after it went free to play all of a  sudden i was averaging hundreds if not  thousands of viewers during my streams  and i started a tick tock channel where  i'd give like one minute tips that  grossed over 200 000 followers within  just a couple of months i was providing  a ton of educational content to new  players i provided coaching for all of  my subscribers and i eventually hit 2500  paid subscribers on twitch i even got  partnered on twitch for this insane  super fast growth within the rocket  league community i even met a new girl  that i started dating and got my own  really nice apartment in a local area  everything was really looking good for a  while but as some of you may know rocket  league pretty much completely died  shortly after this i won't say too much  on this i just wasn't a big fan of the  super young toxic player base that i was  basically babysitting in my twitch chat  on a daily basis the last straw for me  with rocket league was when i hosted a  rocket league tournament where the  winner would receive 1 000 in prize  money when i gave the money to the  winner they didn't even say anything  they didn't say thank you nothing they  just took the money and completely  disappeared after this i was pissed off  and i just went back to variety  streaming kind of out of spite just  being mad at that situation and i had  thoughts of just giving up on content  creation altogether after this too my  girlfriend thought this was a really bad  idea she thought i should just keep  streaming rockily because that's what  was working and she started acting  really different toward me we had  planned to move in together soon but it  was apparent that she only liked me for  my success on twitch she was pretty much  a gold digger and we broke up and i lost  my lease on the apartment because we  were going to move into a different  apartment within like a couple weeks i  gave up my lease to be in that apartment  and when she decided not to go through  with it i just lost my place to live  pretty much and i definitely couldn't  afford the three-bedroom apartment that  we were going to rent by myself so my  parents were kind enough to let me move  back in with them things were looking  pretty bad and i did not know what to do  then i saw a trailer for elden ring to  release in early 2022 and i can tell you  that all of my hopes came back i had  played every souls game multiple times  over at this point they were my favorite  games i had ever played but they never  did well while i was streaming or making  content with them unless i was already  solidified in the community which i  definitely was not i had streamed every  souls game but like i said they just  didn't do well but eldon ring was a  completely new game and it sent like  from software was marketing the game  more than they usually did with their  previous titles so i started thinking  that with all my experience making  content up to this point it may have  prepared me enough to get on the ground  running when elden ring released from  software also has a very special place  in my heart i played the souls games  over and over and over again to get me  through some of the darkest times of my  life sort of ironic for games called  dark souls during a dark time in my life  i even bought a ps4 just so i could play  bloodborne and sakiro launched around  this time as well they've all been some  of my favorite games i had ever played  and i was so excited for elden ring to  come out especially after some of the  worst game releases in my lifetime i was  so excited about cyberpunk and was  completely disappointed i was also  excited about the last of us too which  was okay in my mind but was met with  some pretty horrible backlash for the  narrative and rightfully so to be honest  but i knew from software just doesn't  make bad games but if they were going to  make a bad game now would have been the  time it just felt like gaming in general  i was losing my love for gaming i just i  was so disappointed by every new release  that came out for you know all of 2020  all of 2021 i just i just couldn't find  love for gaming at this time but we all  know what happened eldon ring launched  and i had the best gaming experience i  had ever had since i played skyrim i  knew i was playing something special as  soon as i defeated godric walked out the  back of the castle and i got this view  this absolutely blew me away with how  big the game really was it's just so  flush with detail in the combat was  exactly what i wanted with a new souls  game and not to mention the deep lore  within the game that i immediately  wanted to understand [ __ ] it took me  about 58 hours to roll credits in my  first playthrough which wasn't even  close to enough time to experience the  full game i didn't even find melania in  my first playthrough i was just confused  since i saw this red-haired girl in the  trailer  and i never found her in the game so i  knew i hadn't explored the entire game  yet but it was my first time playing so  i just didn't know what was all out  there and neither did anybody else i  decided to start a new series on my  youtube channel called lore hunting  where i would explore certain areas and  would just kind of ask questions about  certain things that i would find in  these areas and in my first episode of  doing this i talked about the husk of  godfrey below stormville castle and the  connection it may have had to godfrey  that we see in the deep root depths at  this time none of us even knew this was  godfrey yet but this video has now  grossed over half a million views and  every video i've made since has done so  much better than i ever could have  imagined and here we are almost 50 000  subscribers and i don't plan on stopping  anytime soon it took a lot of work  pain  and sacrifice to get to this point i  taught myself how to edit on photoshop  and edit videos in premiere to make  videos i watched countless youtube  videos on how to be a better streamer  how i could just do everything better in  general for years i did this and if  there's anything that you can take from  this video  it's that it gets better if you continue  to work hard believe in yourself and do  what you love you can absolutely make  your dreams come true what i'm doing now  is my dream job and i can't thank you  all enough for the opportunity to make  content on a game that i love and i know  all of you love too elden rings saved my  love for gaming and my love for creating  content i appreciate the game and what  it's given me which is why i'll continue  to play it and make content for it so  that's it thank you guys for watching  the video i really hope you enjoyed  something a little different and i'll  see you all in the next one take care  [Music]  you

